# .dev.vars.example
# Application Secrets for Local Worker Development
#
# This file provides secrets to your Worker during local development.
# Copy to .dev.vars and add your secrets:
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# The .dev.vars file is gitignored and safe to store locally.
#
# When to use this file:
#   - Your Worker needs API keys (Claude, OpenAI, etc.)
#   - Your Worker needs database credentials
#   - Your Worker needs any secret values
#
# How it works:
#   - Values are injected into your Worker's `env` parameter
#   - Available during `npm run dev`
#   - For production, use: npx wrangler secret put SECRET_NAME
#
# Note: This file is OPTIONAL. If your Worker doesn't need secrets,
# you don't need to create .dev.vars at all.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Integration (uncomment and fill in as needed)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anthropic API Key (for Claude API integration)
# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com/
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-...

# OpenAI API Key (if using OpenAI integration)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Application Secrets (examples)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database password
# DATABASE_PASSWORD=your-secret-password

# JWT signing secret
# JWT_SECRET=your-jwt-secret

# Session encryption key
# SESSION_SECRET=your-session-secret
